{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139824-how-do-the-mists-work-after-traveling-the-dreaming-in-c20","id":1139824,"title":"How do the Mists work after traveling the Dreaming in C20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-12T20:34:02-07:00","id":1139824,"title":"How do the Mists work after traveling the Dreaming in C20?","content":"After you have returned from a trip into the Far Dreaming and you are now back in Earth, how much can you recall of your adventure in the new C20 book. Not being able to leave the Dreaming with more knowledge than you brought in can really wreck a story centering on your experiences and not the loot you took back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:08:34-07:00","id":1140407,"title":"","content":"I can't remember the section in C20 and am too lazy to look it up, but in previous versions the Mists affected your memory when coming through the Dreaming just like when mortals are affected by the Mists. Yes, this means that the further you go into the Dreaming, the less you remember when you return. It's based on your permanent Banality rating and since most kithain have a relatively low Banality it's not too bad. But it can be kind of frustrating and inconvenient, especially when the player knows much more than their character. In games where I'm ST I've been pretty loose with this rule, and have typically used it in reverse....when they go back into the Dreaming I will sometimes have PCs suddenly remember facts and events that they had forgotten, which can help drive the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T02:43:27-07:00","id":1140463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139824-how-do-the-mists-work-after-traveling-the-dreaming-in-c20?p=1140407#post1140407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In games where I'm ST I've been pretty loose with this rule, and have typically used it in reverse....when they go back into the Dreaming I will sometimes have PCs suddenly remember facts and events that they had forgotten, which can help drive the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a great idea. <br /> <br /> Copied.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T13:52:12-07:00","id":1140628,"title":"","content":"I have a vague recollection that Mists would work just like that by the actual rules. With your memories returning to you as you venture back to the deeper parts of the Dreaming, just like with enchanted mortals, whom are claimed by the Mists as their enchantment wears off but suddenly regain those memories if enchanted again. I'm fairly certain that this is handled in Dreams and Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T23:43:03-07:00","id":1140733,"title":"","content":"So, I went over Dreams and Nightmares and the information relevant to the subject at hand can be found on pages 12-13, 27, 39 and 54-55. And simply put Mists return memories to you the deeper into the Dreaming you go, of past visits and even past lives, and takes them away as you return closer to the Autumn world. Sometimes written notes may survive in parts or in whole while in others Mists may claim them as well. Basically making it a plot device.<br /> <br /> All in all it tends to mean a story set in the Dreaming will be happening in layers as your memories unfold which may even lead to changed allegiances as you remember new things about both your allies and enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-17T12:28:11-07:00","id":1141168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1139824-how-do-the-mists-work-after-traveling-the-dreaming-in-c20?p=1140733#post1140733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I went over Dreams and Nightmares and the information relevant to the subject at hand can be found on pages 12-13, 27, 39 and 54-55. And simply put Mists return memories to you the deeper into the Dreaming you go, of past visits and even past lives, and takes them away as you return closer to the Autumn world. Sometimes written notes may survive in parts or in whole while in others Mists may claim them as well. Basically making it a plot device.<br /> <br /> All in all it tends to mean a story set in the Dreaming will be happening in layers as your memories unfold which may even lead to changed allegiances as you remember new things about both your allies and enemies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great job looking at the page references!<br /> <br /> I love the idea behind this, but it's been tricky for me to use in my games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}